# Model Chain Configuration (canonical)

> This is the single source of truth for model routing across all skills/programs that call the forwarding LLM proxy.
>
> **Endpoint**: `https://tone.nyc.mn/v1` · **Key**: see `api-credentials.env`
>
> **Revision 2026-04-24**: unified chain with `claude-opus-4.7-n` as primary; removed `grok-4.20-0309-reasoning` from active chain (empty-response rate ~70%).

## Available models (validated 2026-04-24)

| Model ID | Type | Cold-start latency | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `claude-opus-4.7-n` | primary, reasoning-capable | 5–10s | **New primary**. Requires few-shot wrapping or system-message to avoid `<l` prefix artifact (~50% without). Ping 8/8. |
| `grok-4.20-0309-non-reasoning` | fast general | <5s | Reliable 8/8 ping, 2–3s median. JSON OK. Structured & freeform both clean. |
| `gpt-5.5` | reasoning-capable | <5s | 7/8 ping (occasional SSL EOF). JSON OK. `reasoning_tokens=10+` baseline. |
| `claude-opus-4.6-n` | backstop, text-first | <10s | Has Notion-AI safety overlay: refuses "Output ONLY" / "override" / system-message coercion. Must use few-shot pattern for JSON. Ping 8/8. |
| `gpt-5.4-n` | reserve | <15s | Internal alias — same backend as gpt-5.5. Use only when primary chain exhausted. |
| `grok-4.20-0309-reasoning` | **off-chain** | N/A | Empty-response rate ~70% via this proxy. Removed from chain pending upstream fix. |

## Unified chain (all task types)

```
claude-opus-4.7-n → grok-4.20-0309-non-reasoning → gpt-5.5 → claude-opus-4.6-n
```

Rationale: Opus 4.7-n at the head gives best reasoning quality; grok-nr is the cheapest reliable fallback (fastest median latency); gpt-5.5 covers structured edge cases; 4.6-n as text-first backstop. All four verified 8/8 ping online (2026-04-24).

Complex-reasoning tasks (team_architect, hypothesis synthesis, literature review) use the same chain — the head model is already top-tier.

## Opus calling recipe (REQUIRED for 4.6-n and 4.7-n)

Both Opus models misbehave under naive calls, with TWO distinct failure modes:

**4.6-n Notion-AI refusal**: rejects system messages and aggressive "Output ONLY"-style instructions.

**4.7-n `<l` content-destruction artifact**: ~60-73% of responses (even WITH a system message) start with `<l`, which is NOT merely a prepended stray token — it REPLACES the first ~9 tokens of intended output, causing real content loss. Example: intended `随机对照试验（RCT）通过随机分组...` is emitted as `<lT）通过随机分组...`, losing `随机对照试验（RC` (verified 2026-04-24, 45-round diagnostic).

### The fix: few-shot priming (user/assistant/user)

Injecting a `(user, assistant)` example pair BEFORE the real user message primes the tokenizer and **eliminates the `<l` artifact (0/15 dirty rate verified)**.

For STRUCTURED output (JSON/schema): `wrap_with_fewshot()` — drops system msg (required for 4.6-n), inserts JSON example:
```python
[example_user, example_assistant, real_user]
```

For GENERAL CHAT (team discussion, literature review, most agent calls): `wrap_chat_messages()` — PRESERVES system msg, inserts generic academic few-shot:
```python
[system_msg?, example_user, example_assistant, real_user]
```
Using example_user="请简要说明什么是同行评审？" / example_assistant="同行评审是学术出版的质量控制机制..."

### Lenient response parser (defense in depth)

After few-shot priming, `<l` should not appear. But the parser still handles:

1. Residual `<l` prefix — `strip_opus_prefix()` removes it
2. Markdown fences on 4.6-n — extract `{...}` from ` ```json...``` ` wrapper
3. Preamble before JSON — find first balanced `{...}` fallback
4. Notion-AI refusal — `is_opus_refusal()` detects and signals cascade fallback

### Framework integration

Canonical helper: `~/.claude/config/opus_helper.py`. Copied into each downstream program.

- **Agno** (scicrew): `make_opus_aware_model(model_id, ...)` returns an `OpusAwareOpenAILike` subclass that auto-injects few-shot at `invoke()`/`ainvoke()` time. Transparent drop-in for `OpenAILike`.
- **CAMEL** (scicamel): before `agent.step()`, call `agent.update_memory(ex_user, OpenAIBackendRole.USER)` + `agent.update_memory(ex_assistant, OpenAIBackendRole.ASSISTANT)`.
- **urllib/OpenAI client** (researchclaw): call `wrap_chat_messages(messages)` before POST; `strip_opus_prefix(content)` after.
- **CrewAI ConeLLM** (scisuper): patched `call()` injects few-shot via `wrap_chat_messages(merged)` when model is Opus.

